    pr_ref:  # d762
    description: "WI-favav's nested-pool resolver was applied to TWO of its call sites and missed at\nleast THREE more. The result: `bakeoff-deep run --pool ~/ALL_REPOS` — the documented\nusage, and the pool every session on this machine uses — dies with FileNotFoundError\nfor any repo living one level down in a collection subdir.\n\nREPRODUCED 2026-09-10, on the way into a directed DEEP cycle:\n\n  $ ./scripts/bakeoff-deep cohort --repos django\n    django   56.3MB  6915 files  [python, javascript]   <- SELECTION resolves it\n  $ ./scripts/bakeoff-deep run\n    FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory:\n      '/home/jgstern_agent/ALL_REPOS/django'            <- RUN does not\n\nCohort selection WRITES the correct absolute path into the cohort metadata:\n  \"path\": \"/home/jgstern_agent/ALL_REPOS/whole_bunch_of_repos/django\"\nand `_run_cohort_repos` then DISCARDS it and re-derives a weaker one.\n\nTHE VIOLATED INVARIANT: a path already resolved by the shared resolver must not be\nre-derived downstream by a naive join. Selection and run must agree by CONSTRUCTION\n— i.e. by calling the same resolver — not by coincidence of pool layout.\n\nENUMERATED ROUTES (grep for `os.path.join(pool_path`, both scripts and both reflect\nscripts), rather than fixing the one that happened to bite:\n\n  scripts/bakeoff-deep:1980           `_run_cohort_repos`      <- BLOCKS run\n  scripts/bakeoff-deep-reflect:893                             <- inside `cycle`\n  scripts/bakeoff-broad-reflect:688                            <- sibling, same shape\n  scripts/bakeoff-deep-reflect:1004   f-string telling the agent `<pool>/<repo_name>/`\n  scripts/bakeoff-broad-reflect:722   same f-string\n\nThe last two are lower severity but the SAME defect: they print a path that does not\nexist, aimed at an agent that will then look in the wrong place.\n\nALREADY CORRECT, and the model to copy: `scripts/bakeoff-broad::_pool_repo_path`\n(line 221) wraps `pool_utils.resolve_repo_path` with a fallback to the naive join so\na genuinely-missing repo still errors as before. `scripts/bakeoff-deep` line 1689\nalready calls the resolver in SELECTION and cites WI-favav in the comment — so the\nfix and its rationale were both present in this very file and the run path still\nmissed them.\n\nWHY THIS MATTERS BEYOND THE CRASH: the reflect site is inside `bakeoff-deep cycle`,\nso a cycle can select repos correctly, analyse them correctly, and then hand the\nreflect agent a wrong source path. A crash is the GOOD failure. A reflect pass\nreading nothing because the path is wrong is the silent one.\n\nFIX: mirror `_pool_repo_path` into `bakeoff-deep` and both reflect scripts, with a\nparity test per script modelled on tests/test_bakeoff_broad_pool_path.py."  # d762
    fields: {}  # d762
